arm: io_submap 32 MiB instead of 8 MiB (ADSP probe panic)

The port maps far more device memory than an iPhone (MDP, GPU, GMU, USB, UFS, TLMM, modem windows, BT, battery, touch); 0300's ADSP probe mapping SMEM partitions ran io_submap out and kmem_alloc(KMA_NOFAIL) panicked ~10 s after boot (boot55, same failure as boot45). 32 MiB is the size osfmk/i386/io_map.c uses; kernel VA is plentiful.

--- a/osfmk/arm/io_map.c
+++ b/osfmk/arm/io_map.c
@@ -62,7 +62,7 @@
 
 extern vm_offset_t virtual_space_start;     /* Next available kernel VA */
 
-#define IO_MAP_SIZE            (8ul << 20)
+#define IO_MAP_SIZE            (32ul << 20)
 
 __startup_data static struct mach_vm_range io_range;
 static SECURITY_READ_ONLY_LATE(vm_map_t) io_submap;
